package periapsis:perseidts;

// ***ITS OWN FILE, AND NOT BECAUSE OF TIDINESS.*** `tools/derive-wit.ts` reads
// the build world with `parseWitDecls`, which is LINE-BASED and world-unaware:
// it collects every `import`/`export` line in the file it is handed. With two
// worlds in `world.wit` it attributed this world's `observe-cluster` to
// `perseid-ts` and refused the build:
//
//     error: the build world declares 1 capability the code never demands:
//            perseid:reconcile/observe-cluster
//
// The refusal was CORRECT about the file it was given and wrong about the world,
// which is the failure mode of a textual parser used as a semantic one. Splitting
// the worlds is the one-line fix; teaching the parser about worlds is the other,
// and is worth doing if a third world ever lands here.

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// THE GOVERNANCE MONITOR — apogeos' gazer-governance check as a Perseid.
//
// A SECOND WORLD IN THE SAME PACKAGE rather than a second example directory:
// it shares this one's `wit/deps`, its toolchain and its SDK import path, and
// the thing worth demonstrating is the CAPABILITY SET, which is the one part
// that differs.
//
// ***IT IMPORTS observe-cluster AND NOT observe.*** That is the whole point of
// the port: the monitor reads two CLUSTER-SCOPED objects, and the namespaced
// read cannot address them - a cluster-scoped object has no namespace for the
// grant to bound, which is why reading one needs its own interface and an
// explicit `spec.reads`.
//
// It imports NO `workloads`: a monitor reports and does not mutate. A world that
// granted it anyway would be admitted and would confer an authority the program
// has no code to use - the widening this contract keeps arguing against.
//
// Must stay in step with `derived/governance.wit`, which derive-wit reads out of
// the Generator yield type in `src/governance-main.ts`. Nothing compares them
// automatically; that gap is documented on `perseid-ts` above and cost a
// component that could not be admitted.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
world governance {
  include wasi:cli/command@0.3.0;

  import perseid:reconcile/observe-cluster@0.1.0;
  import perseid:reconcile/status@0.1.0;

  export perseid:reconcile/step@0.1.0;
  export perseid:reconcile/signal@0.1.0;
}
